<%# Repricing the cart for a new destination changes the shipping line, and with
    it VAT and the Total, on BOTH cart surfaces. The field is mounted in each, so
    each is replaced wholesale rather than patching individual lines: a partial
    update could leave one surface quoting a destination the other had moved on
    from. Both replacements are no-ops where that surface isn't mounted.

    A refusal is reported inside the calculator itself rather than through the
    flash: the flash renders as a bare div in the layout with no id to target,
    and an inline message sits where the customer is already looking. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "drawer_cart_content" do %>
  <%= render "shared/drawer_cart_content" %>
<% end %>

<%= turbo_stream.replace "cart_summary", partial: "cart_items/summary", locals: { cart: Current.cart } %>

<%# The cart page mounts the calculator outside #cart_summary, so its own copy of
    the field (and the note under it) needs replacing separately. The drawer's
    copy came along with drawer_cart_content above.

    `targetable` re-emits the #delivery_calculator id that Turbo matched to get
    here. Without it the field updates once and then goes dead, having replaced
    itself with a copy the next submission has nothing to target. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "delivery_calculator", partial: "cart_items/delivery_calculator",
                         locals: { cart: Current.cart, targetable: true } %>

<%# The cart page's checkout button lives outside both blocks above, and whether
    it is disabled is decided when it renders. Replacing only the totals left it
    stating the previous answer: still disabled after a valid postcode was
    entered (a dead end, with the totals repriced right beside it), or still
    enabled after one was cleared (a checkout the guard then refuses).

    The drawer's button needs no equivalent: it came along with
    drawer_cart_content. A no-op where the cart page isn't mounted. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "cart_checkout", partial: "cart_items/checkout",
                         locals: { cart: Current.cart } %>
